        {"topic": "define_cloud_computing", "question": "Which of the following statements about cloud computing is correct?", "choices": ["Cloud computing requires customers to buy physical servers before they can use it", "Cloud computing lets organizations access computing resources over the internet and pay based on usage", "Cloud computing can only be used for storing files, not for running applications", "Cloud computing eliminates the need for an internet connection"], "answerIndex": 1, "explanation": "A defining characteristic of cloud computing is on-demand, pay-for-use access to resources delivered over the internet."},
