        {"topic": "encryption_and_key_management", "question": "What security and compliance benefit does centralized key management provide?", "choices": ["It eliminates the need for any access control", "It allows control over who can access keys, supports key rotation, and enables auditing of usage", "It removes the need for encryption entirely", "It only benefits large enterprises, not smaller organizations"], "answerIndex": 1, "explanation": "Centralized key management supports controlling access, rotating keys over time, and auditing key/secret usage for compliance."},
